From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: openEuler RISC-V Package Automation <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] cmake: exclude generated compiler probes

The recursive source glob can see CMake's generated compiler-identification
source when the build directory has a toolchain-derived name. Exclude
CMakeFiles explicitly so the probe's main function is not linked into the
application.

Patch-Source: openEuler RISC-V package CI failure analysis
Patch-License: MIT
Upstream-Status: Not Submitted (automated upstream writes are not authorized)
---
 CMakeLists.txt | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -20,6 +20,7 @@ endif()
 # collect all source files recursively, excluding build directory
 file(GLOB_RECURSE SOURCES CONFIGURE_DEPENDS "${CMAKE_SOURCE_DIR}/*.cpp")
 list(FILTER SOURCES EXCLUDE REGEX ".*/.*build.*/.*")
+list(FILTER SOURCES EXCLUDE REGEX ".*/CMakeFiles/.*")
 
 # creating executable
 add_executable(${PROJECT_NAME} ${SOURCES})
-- 
